.el .ds Aq '
.TH handoverctl 1  "handoverctl 0.1.0" 
.SH NAME
handoverctl \- Inspect and control Handover
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBhandoverctl\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Inspect and control Handover devices through the local handoverd daemon.
.PP
Commands that change remote state report acceptance, not completion. The daemon owns authoritative state; this CLI rebuilds its view from a fresh snapshot on each run. handoverd must be running and reachable over $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/handover/handoverd.sock.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
handoverctl\-devices(1)
List devices known to handoverd
.TP
handoverctl\-native(1)
Inspect and manage native Android pairing and device commands
.TP
handoverctl\-notifications(1)
List active remote notifications from the daemon snapshot
.TP
handoverctl\-contacts(1)
List or request an on\-demand native contacts snapshot
.TP
handoverctl\-media(1)
List media sessions, or send one playback command
.TP
handoverctl\-monitor(1)
Print live normalized device and notification changes
.TP
handoverctl\-send\-url(1)
Send a URL to one paired device
.TP
handoverctl\-notify(1)
Send a notification to one native phone
.TP
handoverctl\-clipboard(1)
Set the clipboard on one native phone
.TP
handoverctl\-send\-file(1)
Send one local file to a paired device
.TP
handoverctl\-screensaver(1)
Control the desktop idle inhibitor: inhibit, release, or follow
.TP
handoverctl\-clipboard\-mirror(1)
Get or set Linux\-to\-phone background clipboard mirroring (off by default)
.TP
handoverctl\-clipboard\-history(1)
List, pin, copy, and clear phone\-to\-Linux clipboard history
.TP
handoverctl\-cancel\-share(1)
Cancel a queued native share that has not started streaming
.TP
handoverctl\-custom(1)
List or run allowlisted desktop commands
.TP
handoverctl\-calls(1)
Print current normalized call state for one device
.TP
handoverctl\-messages(1)
Inspect and use messaging accounts and conversations
.TP
handoverctl\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH EXTRA
Exit status: 0 on success, 1 on any error (daemon unreachable, unknown device, rejected request).
Run `handoverctl <command> \-\-help` for per\-command detail.
.SH VERSION
v0.1.0
